# The instance file — where the real vault lives on THIS host.
#
# Copy to ~/.hermes/sync-bridge.env (or point SYNC_BRIDGE_ENV at it) and edit. It lives OUTSIDE
# the repo on purpose: the repo's own defaults are placeholders, so a clone can never write to
# somebody's real vault by accident, and publishing the repo can never publish your paths.
#
# Who reads it:
#   mac/ingest.py                 the consumer (the 1-minute loop)
#   mac/kanban-card.py            the board tooling
#   mac/kanban-archive-roll.py    the nightly filing
#   mac/kanban-archive-roll-cron.sh
#   mac/deploy.sh                 resolves it the same way before installing
#   docker/docker-kanban-card.py  the board tooling on the producing host (the vault id)
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   1. an explicit argument (--vault) or the process environment
#   2. this file
#   3. the repo's placeholder default (/Volumes/Data/vault)
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line, `#` starts a comment, quotes are optional.

VAULT_ROOT=/path/to/your/vault

# The Hatchdoor vault that holds the Kanban board, for docker/docker-kanban-card.py. Find it with
# the Hatchdoor `list_vaults` tool; it is the id of the vault your board note lives in.
# HATCHDOOR_VAULT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Optional: the archive roller's vault, if it is not the same tree as VAULT_ROOT.
# KANBAN_VAULT=/path/to/your/vault

# Optional: point SYNC_BRIDGE_ENV somewhere else entirely.
# SYNC_BRIDGE_ENV=/path/to/sync-bridge.env
